{% include "loading" %}


<style>
  .article-collection-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    column-gap: 16px;
    row-gap: 20px;
    padding: 20px 40px 40px 40px;
  }
  
  .graphics-article-title {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 20px;
    padding: 43px 20px 0 20px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 440px;
    line-height: 26px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    opacity: 1;
    -moz-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -webkit-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -o-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    -ms-transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
    transition: all .3s ease-in-out;
  }
  
  .centered-article-text {
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  
  .blog-img-caption {
    top: 10px;
  }
  
  .gallery {
    min-height: 10px;
  }
  
  .post-grid-three-column {
    display: grid; 
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    column-gap: 10px;
    row-gap: 12px;
    padding: 0px 40px 0px 40px;
  }
  .post-grid-item-1 {
    grid-column: span 1;
    display: flex;  
    align-self: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .graphics-article-title {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 26px;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 80px 20px 0px;
      font-weight: 500;
      max-width: 580px;
    }  
    .article-collection-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      column-gap: 16px;
      row-gap: 20px;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    .post-grid-three-column {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        padding: 0px 10px;
    }
    .post-grid-item-1 img {
      padding: 0px;
    }
  }
</style>

<div class="graphics-article-title" >
 {{ article.title }}
</div>
<span class="new-centered-article-text">
Camp Hero is a weird place. It sits at the very end of the Long Island in Montauk and was commissioned by the US Army in 1942 as a coastal defense station disguised as a fishing village. It inspired elements of the creative direction of SS16, and took the naming convention for one of the first pieces of clothing we ever designed, the Camp Hero Short. 
</span>

<div class="max-width-1200" style="opacity: 1;">
    <img class="center-single ss16-preview" src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0664/2387/files/CHSS-25.jpg?v=1628016645">
</div>

<span class="new-centered-article-text">
    The Camp Hero Shorts are based on a classic volley short design. The inseam is longer than our Site Short with a more narrow leg opening which is typical of the volley design and makes it less of a baggy wide leg swim trunk. It is designed to function as an active short but also a swim short because of quick dry elements of the four way stretch main body fabric and every pocket has a generous mesh drainage system. 
</span>

